{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1775216130,"nonce":"szEaUaucz4XGSWz8Jtv63LuSTR0=","message":"💭 The current `TG_HTTP_TIMEOUT_S=5` and `TG_LONG_POLL_TIMEOUT_S=1` mean the request should complete in about 2s normally (1s long poll + network). The worst case is 5s. The shutdown check before `poll_all()` and at the top of `poll_all()` means we only block for the duration of an in-flight request. With `TG_HTTP_TIMEOUT_S=5`, worst case is 5s which is acceptable for the \"1-2 seconds\" target when combined with the 1s long poll. But let me reduce `TG_HTTP_TIMEOUT_S` to 3s to be tighter — 1s long poll + 2s margin:","files":null}]}